<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ptolemy II Philadelphus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">309–246 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ptolemy II Philadelphus was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> from 283 to 246 BCE, born on Kos. He expanded the Library and Museum of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> and extended Ptolemaic power through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>, where the Nesiotic League honoured him, and on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, where he refounded Marion as Arsinoe. He eventually made peace with his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magas-of-cyrene">Magas of Cyrene</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ptolemy-ii-philadelphus.jpg" alt="Ptolemy II Philadelphus" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ptolemy_II_MAN_Napoli_Inv5600.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
